cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this manuscript or Lean 4 formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "On the Exceptional Set in the Binary Goldbach Problem in Arithmetic Progressions of Arbitrary Modulus under GRH and Its Formalization in Lean 4"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lin
    given-names: KenRui
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Guangzhou, China"
    email: "longinuslkr@gmail.com"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - binary Goldbach problem
  - exceptional set
  - arithmetic progressions
  - Generalized Riemann Hypothesis
  - Hardy-Littlewood circle method
  - smoothed explicit formula
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
abstract: >-
  Assuming the Generalized Riemann Hypothesis (GRH) for all primitive Dirichlet
  L-functions, we prove a uniform upper bound on the exceptional set E_r(X; b_1, b_2)
  for the binary Goldbach problem with both prime summands restricted to arbitrary
  coprime residue classes modulo any positive integer r >= 1, together with a
  complete zero-sorry formalization in Lean 4 / Mathlib v4.36.0 (13 files, 13,595 lines)
  depending solely on [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].
